 @playdoe3275  our lymph glands get clogged due to sedentary lifestyle usually. We gotta get up & move!!! If we start having nerve problems due to trauma...it’s hard to get up & move without more pain. Some people need certain meds to help the nervous system so they can get up & move & then the lymph glands can get to clearing out. Certain foods, drinks & supplements do help but not like certain prescriptions can. I had a great doctor, nutritionist, trainer & a chiropractor once upon a time & they all taught me so much abt the anatomy of the human body. I also have read a lot of medical books since then & watched many videos on this subject because I want to completely understand it! I have had these issues most of my life & I’m almost 60! So there’s been a bunch of research I’ve personally done, a bunch of experimenting on my body from other doctors too on me, especially since 2006. Like I wrote, I’m no doctor or nurse or any healthcare expert. I’ve just been researching these types of issues most of my life for myself & from being nosey with other patients. I want to understand it all because for many years it was a mystery to me & unless someone has these types of health issues & have been blessed enough to of ever had good healthcare providers in their life (needle in a haystack lemme tell ya!), then they won’t be able to completely understand it. 
Like now, there’s so much info abt diabetes & people live a long life with diabetes now because of research. I had an aunt (very close to) died in the early 90’s from complications of being diabetic. Her doctor had basically been using her as a guinea pig! He didn’t know diddly abt the disease but he didn’t want to refer her to a specialist either! Me & my family all wanted to take her to Dallas to a specialist & her doctor had her so brainwashed for his own greed that she wouldn’t go. I would go to the college & check out medical books from the library to show her but that quack had her so brainwashed believing everything he said that she wouldn’t listen to the truth. It’s was sad. She died at 66 after losing both her legs in her 50’s. 
So research, research, research & then research some more. If something gets confusing don’t give up! Find the answer. Knowledge is worth our health!
